From 3119d7cc17b7a432cbf10c52043a5115e5478948 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garv <garvagnihotri22@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(home): add the Loophole home screen to the empty editor

- port of Void's EmptyEditorHome.tsx as plain DOM: the logo, the tagline ("Beyond Code Completion" /
  "An Agentic AI IDE") and a keyboard shortcut list, in the watermark of an empty editor group.
- editorGroupWatermark.ts: replace the stock entries (Open Chat, Open Recent, ...) with the Loophole list from
  the new emptyEditorHome.ts, and rebuild the list whenever keybindings change, since the agent extension
  registers its keybindings after startup.
- the AI entries point at the Loophole agent (Kilo) commands instead of Void's Ctrl+L / Ctrl+K actions:
  Chat (kilo-code.new.focusChatInput), Suggest Edits (...autocomplete.generateSuggestions, Ctrl+L),
  Add to Context (kilo-code.new.addToContext, Ctrl+K Ctrl+A) and Agent Manager.
- only shortcuts that really have a keybinding are listed, so unbinding a key removes the row.
- the logo is the Loophole mark as a CSS mask in the foreground color instead of the faint letterpress image.
